"""Optional web interface: a streaming chat + a live ``/config`` panel (FastAPI).

Generated only when ``interfaces.web`` is enabled. ``/chat`` streams the loop's
progress over Server-Sent Events by listening on the existing :class:`Hooks`
extension point — the loop itself is untouched. ``/config`` reads and edits the
*runtime behavioral* config (prompts, enabled tools, context, sampling, per-LLM
pricing + cost limits) and never exposes secrets: profiles only carry env-var
NAMES. A Save applies the
edit to the running process AND persists it back to ``config.yaml`` (comments
preserved, via ruamel.yaml), so a restart keeps it instead of reverting to the
file. Structural config (which interfaces / modules exist) is not editable here.

Run it with ``{{ project_slug }} serve`` or ``uvicorn``.
"""

